# Skill compatibility (global hard rule)

## Authority order

1. Global rules  
2. `requirements-manager` + `.cursor/REQUIREMENTS.md`  
3. `adaptive-workflow` (skip on Tiny)  
4. Domain skills (implement / debug / eng review)  
5. `acceptance-review` — sole Pass / Passed-with-follow-up / Fail  

## Do not run as peer authorities

- Do not use brainstorming HARD-GATE, llm-council (default), verification-loop-as-Pass, PM Butler Gatekeeper/Sculptor, OpenCastle always-on gates, or fullstack-forge-all alongside this pipeline.
- gstack `qa` / `design-review` may fix code only in **impl/rework**, not as Pass.
- For UI evidence into acceptance prefer `browser-qa` or `qa-only`.

## Recipes

Follow combinations in:

`~/.cursor/SKILL_COMPATIBILITY_AND_COMBOS.md`

(project `.cursor/` copy is fine if present). Pick one recipe per task set; do not stack opposing explore/plan/accept skills.
